IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc10-libel`

-- ccc10-tests-libel.l4 -- tests for ccc10-libel.l4 (ss 297 to 317). Expected values are written by hand from the text, beside each assertion.
-- (The assertion lines were laid out by a script from a table of hand-written rows, each carrying its expected value and its basis in the text; the script reads no encoding output.)

`s 300 fixture: the general summary conviction penalty` MEANS Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`
GIVEN maximum IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 300 fixture: on indictment at most` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` maximum), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `s 297 -- Definition of newspaper`

#ASSERT `s 297 the publication is a newspaper` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 31 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- limb 1: news, printed for sale, published periodically, at intervals not exceeding thirty-one days
#ASSERT `s 297 the publication is a newspaper` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 32 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- limb 1: an interval of 32 days exceeds thirty-one
#ASSERT `s 297 the publication is a newspaper` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 7 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- limb 1: a weekly paper
#ASSERT `s 297 the publication is a newspaper` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 31 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- limb 1: no public news, intelligence or reports of events
#ASSERT `s 297 the publication is a newspaper` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 31 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- limb 1: not printed for sale
#ASSERT `s 297 the publication is a newspaper` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 31 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- limb 1: not published periodically or in parts or numbers
#ASSERT `s 297 the publication is a newspaper` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 31 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not a paper, magazine or periodical
#ASSERT `s 297 the publication is a newspaper` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 31 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- limb 2: printed to be dispersed and made public, at intervals not exceeding thirty-one days, advertisements exclusively or principally
#ASSERT `s 297 the publication is a newspaper` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 7 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- limb 2: weekly
#ASSERT `s 297 the publication is a newspaper` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 32 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- limb 2: more than thirty-one days
#ASSERT `s 297 the publication is a newspaper` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 31 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- limb 2: no advertisements
#ASSERT `s 297 the publication is a newspaper` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 31 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- limb 2: not printed to be dispersed and made public
#ASSERT `s 297 the definition applies in the section` (`Provision of the Code` OF 303, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "In sections 303, 304 and 308": section 303
#ASSERT `s 297 the definition applies in the section` (`Provision of the Code` OF 304, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "In sections 303, 304 and 308": section 304
#ASSERT `s 297 the definition applies in the section` (`Provision of the Code` OF 308, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "In sections 303, 304 and 308": section 308
#ASSERT `s 297 the definition applies in the section` (`Provision of the Code` OF 305, "") EQUALS NOTHING   -- "In sections 303, 304 and 308": section 305 is not one of the three
#ASSERT `s 297 the definition applies in the section` (`Provision of the Code` OF 307, "") EQUALS NOTHING   -- "In sections 303, 304 and 308": section 307
#ASSERT `s 297 the definition applies in the section` (`Provision of the Code` OF 478, "") EQUALS NOTHING   -- "In sections 303, 304 and 308": section 478 (the definition is stated for sections 303, 304 and 308)
#ASSERT `s 297 the definition applies in the section` (`Provision of the Code` OF 309, "") EQUALS NOTHING   -- "In sections 303, 304 and 308": section 309
§ `ss 298 and 299 -- Defamatory libel and publishing`

#ASSERT `s 298(1) the matter is a defamatory libel` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- published without lawful justification or excuse, likely to injure the reputation
#ASSERT `s 298(1) the matter is a defamatory libel` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- published without justification, designed to insult
#ASSERT `s 298(1) the matter is a defamatory libel` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- both limbs
#ASSERT `s 298(1) the matter is a defamatory libel` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither limb: "A defamatory libel is matter published ... that is likely to injure ... or that is designed to insult"
#ASSERT `s 298(1) the matter is a defamatory libel` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- there is lawful justification or excuse
#ASSERT `s 298(1) the matter is a defamatory libel` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not published
#ASSERT `s 298(2) a defamatory libel may be expressed in this manner and medium` `s 298(2) directly` `s 298(2)(a) in words legibly marked on any substance` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- directly, in words legibly marked on any substance
#ASSERT `s 298(2) a defamatory libel may be expressed in this manner and medium` `s 298(2) by insinuation` `s 298(2)(b) by any object signifying a defamatory libel otherwise than by words` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- by insinuation, by an object
#ASSERT `s 298(2) a defamatory libel may be expressed in this manner and medium` `s 298(2) by irony` `s 298(2)(a) in words legibly marked on any substance` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- by irony, in words
#ASSERT `s 298(2) a defamatory libel may be expressed in this manner and medium` `s 298(2) in another manner` `s 298(2)(a) in words legibly marked on any substance` EQUALS NOTHING   -- another manner: "may be expressed" does not close the list
#ASSERT `s 298(2) a defamatory libel may be expressed in this manner and medium` `s 298(2) directly` `s 298(2) in another medium` EQUALS NOTHING   -- another medium: the list is not closed
#ASSERT `s 299 the person publishes a libel` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a): exhibits it in public
#ASSERT `s 299 the person publishes a libel` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b): causes it to be read or seen
#ASSERT `s 299 the person publishes a libel` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c): shows or delivers it with intent that it be read or seen by another
#ASSERT `s 299 the person publishes a libel` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- none of (a) to (c): "A person publishes a libel when he"
§ `ss 300 to 302 -- Offences`

#ASSERT `s 300 the person is guilty of the offence of publishing a defamatory libel that they know is false` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a defamatory libel published by the person who knows it is false; no defence applies
#ASSERT `s 300 the person is guilty of the offence of publishing a defamatory libel that they know is false` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the defences do not apply
#ASSERT `s 300 the person is guilty of the offence of publishing a defamatory libel that they know is false` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- does not know it is false: section 301 instead
#ASSERT `s 300 the person is guilty of the offence of publishing a defamatory libel that they know is false` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "No person shall be deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only that": a defence applies
#ASSERT `s 300 the person is guilty of the offence of publishing a defamatory libel that they know is false` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a defamatory libel under s 298(1)
#ASSERT `s 300 the person is guilty of the offence of publishing a defamatory libel that they know is false` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- s 298(1) not determined
#ASSERT `s 300 the person is guilty of the offence of publishing a defamatory libel that they know is false` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a publication under s 299
#ASSERT `s 300 the person is guilty of the offence of publishing a defamatory libel that they know is false` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- s 299 not determined
#ASSERT `s 300 the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`   -- (a) or (b)
#ASSERT `s 300 the punishment` `by indictment` `s 300 fixture: the general summary conviction penalty` EQUALS `s 300 fixture: on indictment at most` `five years`   -- (a): "not more than five years"
#ASSERT `s 300 the punishment` `on summary conviction` `s 300 fixture: the general summary conviction penalty` EQUALS `s 300 fixture: the general summary conviction penalty`   -- (b): s 787(1)
#ASSERT `s 301 the person is guilty of the offence of publishing a defamatory libel` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- publishes a defamatory libel
#ASSERT `s 301 the person is guilty of the offence of publishing a defamatory libel` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a defence applies
#ASSERT `s 301 the person is guilty of the offence of publishing a defamatory libel` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a defamatory libel
#ASSERT `s 301 the person is guilty of the offence of publishing a defamatory libel` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a publication
#ASSERT `s 301 the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`   -- (a) or (b)
#ASSERT `s 301 the punishment` `by indictment` `s 300 fixture: the general summary conviction penalty` EQUALS `s 300 fixture: on indictment at most` `two years`   -- (a): "not more than two years"
#ASSERT `s 301 the punishment` `on summary conviction` `s 300 fixture: the general summary conviction penalty` EQUALS `s 300 fixture: the general summary conviction penalty`   -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 302(1) the person commits the offence of extortion by libel` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- intent (a) to extort money, publishes or threatens
#ASSERT `s 302(1) the person commits the offence of extortion by libel` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- intent (b) to induce an appointment or office, publishes or threatens
#ASSERT `s 302(1) the person commits the offence of extortion by libel` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no publishing, threatening or offering to abstain
#ASSERT `s 302(1) the person commits the offence of extortion by libel` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither intent
#ASSERT `s 302(2) the person commits the offence of publishing a libel after a refusal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- as the result of a refusal, publishes or threatens to publish
#ASSERT `s 302(2) the person commits the offence of publishing a libel after a refusal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no publishing or threat
#ASSERT `s 302(2) the person commits the offence of publishing a libel after a refusal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not as the result of a refusal
#ASSERT `s 302(3) the person who commits an offence under this section is guilty of the offence` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an offence under (1)
#ASSERT `s 302(3) the person who commits an offence under this section is guilty of the offence` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an offence under (2)
#ASSERT `s 302(3) the person who commits an offence under this section is guilty of the offence` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no offence under this section shown
#ASSERT `s 302(3) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`   -- (a) or (b)
#ASSERT `s 302(3) the punishment` `by indictment` `s 300 fixture: the general summary conviction penalty` EQUALS `s 300 fixture: on indictment at most` `five years`   -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 302(3) the punishment` `on summary conviction` `s 300 fixture: the general summary conviction penalty` EQUALS `s 300 fixture: the general summary conviction penalty`   -- (b)
§ `ss 303 and 304 -- Newspapers and sellers`

#ASSERT `s 303(1) the proprietor of a newspaper is deemed to publish the defamatory matter` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- deemed to publish defamatory matter inserted and published therein
#ASSERT `s 303(1) the proprietor of a newspaper is deemed to publish the defamatory matter` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless he proves that the defamatory matter was inserted ... without his knowledge and without negligence"
#ASSERT `s 303(1) the proprietor of a newspaper is deemed to publish the defamatory matter` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- proof of no knowledge alone does not suffice: both are needed
#ASSERT `s 303(1) the proprietor of a newspaper is deemed to publish the defamatory matter` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- proof of no negligence alone does not suffice
#ASSERT `s 303(1) the proprietor of a newspaper is deemed to publish the defamatory matter` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a newspaper as s 297 has it
#ASSERT `s 303(1) the proprietor of a newspaper is deemed to publish the defamatory matter` NOTHING TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- s 297 not determined
#ASSERT `s 303(1) the proprietor of a newspaper is deemed to publish the defamatory matter` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not the proprietor
#ASSERT `s 303(1) the proprietor of a newspaper is deemed to publish the defamatory matter` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not inserted and published in the newspaper
#ASSERT `s 303(2) the insertion is deemed not to be negligence on the part of the proprietor` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- general authority to manage; the insertion is deemed not negligence
#ASSERT `s 303(2) the insertion is deemed not to be negligence on the part of the proprietor` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless it is proved that (a) he intended the general authority to include authority to insert defamatory matter"
#ASSERT `s 303(2) the insertion is deemed not to be negligence on the part of the proprietor` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "or (b) he continued to confer general authority after he knew"
#ASSERT `s 303(2) the insertion is deemed not to be negligence on the part of the proprietor` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no general authority given
#ASSERT `s 303(2) the insertion is deemed not to be negligence on the part of the proprietor` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no insertion by that person
#ASSERT `s 303(3) the seller of a number or part of a newspaper is not deemed to publish the defamatory libel by reason only of the sale` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- only sells; does not know
#ASSERT `s 303(3) the seller of a number or part of a newspaper is not deemed to publish the defamatory libel by reason only of the sale` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless he knows that the number or part contains defamatory matter"
#ASSERT `s 303(3) the seller of a number or part of a newspaper is not deemed to publish the defamatory libel by reason only of the sale` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "or that defamatory matter is habitually contained in the newspaper"
#ASSERT `s 303(3) the seller of a number or part of a newspaper is not deemed to publish the defamatory libel by reason only of the sale` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not by reason only of the sale
#ASSERT `s 304(1) the seller of a book, magazine, pamphlet or other thing is not deemed to publish the defamatory libel by reason only of the sale` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- sells a thing other than a newspaper, does not know at the time of the sale
#ASSERT `s 304(1) the seller of a book, magazine, pamphlet or other thing is not deemed to publish the defamatory libel by reason only of the sale` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "if, at the time of the sale, he does not know": he knew
#ASSERT `s 304(1) the seller of a book, magazine, pamphlet or other thing is not deemed to publish the defamatory libel by reason only of the sale` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a newspaper: outside "other than a newspaper" (section 303(3))
#ASSERT `s 304(1) the seller of a book, magazine, pamphlet or other thing is not deemed to publish the defamatory libel by reason only of the sale` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- s 297 not determined
#ASSERT `s 304(1) the seller of a book, magazine, pamphlet or other thing is not deemed to publish the defamatory libel by reason only of the sale` (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not by reason only of the sale
#ASSERT `s 304(2) the employer is deemed not to publish the defamatory matter contained in the thing sold` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a servant sells in the course of employment: the employer is deemed not to publish
#ASSERT `s 304(2) the employer is deemed not to publish the defamatory matter contained in the thing sold` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless it is proved that the employer authorized the sale knowing that (a) defamatory matter was contained therein"
#ASSERT `s 304(2) the employer is deemed not to publish the defamatory matter contained in the thing sold` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "or (b) defamatory matter was habitually contained therein, in the case of a periodical"
#ASSERT `s 304(2) the employer is deemed not to publish the defamatory matter contained in the thing sold` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a newspaper: outside "other than a newspaper"
#ASSERT `s 304(2) the employer is deemed not to publish the defamatory matter contained in the thing sold` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no sale by a servant in the course of employment
§ `ss 305 to 307 -- Proceedings of courts and of the legislatures`

#ASSERT `s 305 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the matter in the proceeding or inquiry` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a): in a proceeding before a court exercising judicial authority
#ASSERT `s 305 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the matter in the proceeding or inquiry` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b): in an inquiry under the authority of an Act
#ASSERT `s 305 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the matter in the proceeding or inquiry` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither
#ASSERT `s 306 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the petition or paper` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a): publishes to the Senate, House of Commons or legislature matter in a petition
#ASSERT `s 306 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the petition or paper` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b): publishes by order or under the authority of the Senate
#ASSERT `s 306 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the petition or paper` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c): an extract, in good faith and without ill-will
#ASSERT `s 306 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the petition or paper` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (c) without good faith and absence of ill-will: outside the limb
#ASSERT `s 306 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the petition or paper` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- none of (a) to (c)
#ASSERT `s 307(1) the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the fair report or fair comment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a fair report, in good faith, for the information of the public
#ASSERT `s 307(1) the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the fair report or fair comment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- in good faith, any fair comment on such proceedings
#ASSERT `s 307(1) the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the fair report or fair comment` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither
#ASSERT `s 307(2) section 307 does not apply to the person who publishes the report` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a report of evidence on a marriage or divorce petition, published without leave
#ASSERT `s 307(2) section 307 does not apply to the person who publishes the report` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- contrary to a rule, order or practice of the House
#ASSERT `s 307(2) section 307 does not apply to the person who publishes the report` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "if the report is published without authority ... or is contrary to any rule": neither (a failed "if")
#ASSERT `s 307(2) section 307 does not apply to the person who publishes the report` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a report of evidence on a petition or bill relating to marriage or divorce
#ASSERT `s 307 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the fair report or fair comment, after subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- immunity applies, no exception
#ASSERT `s 307 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the fair report or fair comment, after subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "This section does not apply to a person who publishes a report of evidence"
#ASSERT `s 307 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the fair report or fair comment, after subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- the exception is not determined
#ASSERT `s 307 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the fair report or fair comment, after subsection (2)` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- the immunity is not determined
#ASSERT `s 307 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the fair report or fair comment, after subsection (2)` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the exception applies whatever (1) says
§ `ss 308 to 315 -- Fair reports, public benefit, fair comment, truth, invitation, inquiries, information and redress`

#ASSERT `s 308 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the fair report of the public meeting` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- all four conditions
#ASSERT `s 308 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the fair report of the public meeting` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a): the meeting is not lawfully convened for a lawful purpose and open to the public
#ASSERT `s 308 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the fair report of the public meeting` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b): the report is not fair and accurate
#ASSERT `s 308 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the fair report of the public meeting` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (c): not for the public benefit
#ASSERT `s 308 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the fair report of the public meeting` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (d): he refuses to publish a reasonable explanation or contradiction
#ASSERT `s 308 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the fair report of the public meeting` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a fair report in good faith of a public meeting
#ASSERT `s 308 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the fair report of the public meeting` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in a newspaper as s 297 has it
#ASSERT `s 308 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the fair report of the public meeting` NOTHING TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- s 297 not determined
#ASSERT `s 309 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing matter believed true that is relevant to a subject of public interest` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- believes on reasonable grounds it is true; relevant to a subject of public interest
#ASSERT `s 309 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing matter believed true that is relevant to a subject of public interest` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not relevant to a subject of public interest whose discussion is for the public benefit
#ASSERT `s 309 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing matter believed true that is relevant to a subject of public interest` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no reasonable belief that it is true
#ASSERT `s 310 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing fair comments` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a): fair comments on the public conduct of a person who takes part in public affairs
#ASSERT `s 310 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing fair comments` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b): on a published work, confined to criticism
#ASSERT `s 310 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing fair comments` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b): "if the comments are confined to criticism thereof": they are not
#ASSERT `s 310 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing fair comments` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a) holds although (b)'s condition fails
#ASSERT `s 310 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing fair comments` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither (a) nor (b)
#ASSERT `s 311 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel where the person proves the publication was for the public benefit and the matter was true` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- proves both
#ASSERT `s 311 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel where the person proves the publication was for the public benefit and the matter was true` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "where he proves that ... and that the matter itself was true": not proved true
#ASSERT `s 311 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel where the person proves the publication was for the public benefit and the matter was true` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not proved for the public benefit
#ASSERT `s 311 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel where the person proves the publication was for the public benefit and the matter was true` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither proved: this section gives no defence on these facts
#ASSERT `s 312 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing on invitation or challenge, or to refute` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a): on invitation or challenge; believes true; relevant; not exceeding
#ASSERT `s 312 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing on invitation or challenge, or to refute` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b): necessary to refute
#ASSERT `s 312 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing on invitation or challenge, or to refute` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "if he believes that the defamatory matter is true": he does not
#ASSERT `s 312 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing on invitation or challenge, or to refute` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not relevant to the invitation, challenge or refutation
#ASSERT `s 312 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing on invitation or challenge, or to refute` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- exceeds what is reasonably sufficient in the circumstances
#ASSERT `s 312 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing on invitation or challenge, or to refute` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither (a) nor (b)
#ASSERT `s 313 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing in answer to inquiries` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- all four conditions
#ASSERT `s 313 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing in answer to inquiries` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a): not in good faith for the purpose of giving information in answer to the inquiries
#ASSERT `s 313 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing in answer to inquiries` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b): he does not believe it is true
#ASSERT `s 313 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing in answer to inquiries` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (c): not relevant to the inquiries
#ASSERT `s 313 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing in answer to inquiries` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (d): exceeds what is reasonably sufficient
#ASSERT `s 313 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing in answer to inquiries` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a publication in answer to inquiries by a person with an interest
#ASSERT `s 314 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of giving information to a person interested` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c): the matter is true
#ASSERT `s 314 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of giving information to a person interested` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c): not true, but without ill-will and in the belief on reasonable grounds that it is true
#ASSERT `s 314 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of giving information to a person interested` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (c): not true, without ill-will but without a belief on reasonable grounds
#ASSERT `s 314 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of giving information to a person interested` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (c): not true, with ill-will
#ASSERT `s 314 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of giving information to a person interested` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a): the conduct is not reasonable in the circumstances
#ASSERT `s 314 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of giving information to a person interested` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b): not relevant to the subject-matter
#ASSERT `s 314 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of giving information to a person interested` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a publication to give information to a person with an interest
#ASSERT `s 315 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing in good faith to seek redress of a wrong` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a), (b) and (c)
#ASSERT `s 315 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing in good faith to seek redress of a wrong` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a): he does not believe that the matter is true
#ASSERT `s 315 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing in good faith to seek redress of a wrong` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b): not relevant to the remedy or redress sought
#ASSERT `s 315 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing in good faith to seek redress of a wrong` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (c): exceeds what is reasonably sufficient
#ASSERT `s 315 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing in good faith to seek redress of a wrong` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a publication in good faith to seek remedy or redress
§ `s 316 -- Proving publication by order of the legislature`

#ASSERT `s 316(1) the accused may, at any stage of the proceedings, adduce evidence that the matter was contained in a paper published by order of the legislature` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an accused alleged to have published; evidence to prove the paper
#ASSERT `s 316(1) the accused may, at any stage of the proceedings, adduce evidence that the matter was contained in a paper published by order of the legislature` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- evidence for another purpose: the grant is limited by its own wording
#ASSERT `s 316(1) the accused may, at any stage of the proceedings, adduce evidence that the matter was contained in a paper published by order of the legislature` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an accused alleged to have published a defamatory libel
#ASSERT `s 316(2) the court shall direct a verdict of not guilty to be entered and shall discharge the accused` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- satisfied at any stage that the matter was contained in a paper published by order
#ASSERT `s 316(2) the court shall direct a verdict of not guilty to be entered and shall discharge the accused` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not satisfied: the "Where" fails
#ASSERT `s 316(3) the certificate is conclusive evidence that the matter was contained in a paper published by order of the legislature` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a certificate under the hand of the Speaker or clerk to that effect
#ASSERT `s 316(3) the certificate is conclusive evidence that the matter was contained in a paper published by order of the legislature` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a certificate to another effect
#ASSERT `s 316(3) the certificate is conclusive evidence that the matter was contained in a paper published by order of the legislature` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not under the hand of the Speaker or clerk
#ASSERT `ss 303 to 316 a provision says the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel` (LIST (JUST FALSE), NOTHING, (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- one provision shields the person
#ASSERT `ss 303 to 316 a provision says the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel` (LIST (JUST FALSE), NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no provision shields: not covered (other justification is not excluded)
#ASSERT `ss 303 to 316 a provision says the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel` (LIST (JUST TRUE), (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- two provisions
#ASSERT `ss 303 to 316 a provision says the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel` (EMPTY) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no provision considered
§ `s 317 -- Verdicts in cases of defamatory libel`

#ASSERT `s 317 the jury may give a general verdict of guilty or not guilty on the whole matter put in issue on the indictment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a plea of not guilty on trial of an indictment for publishing a defamatory libel; the jury is sworn
#ASSERT `s 317 the jury may give a general verdict of guilty or not guilty on the whole matter put in issue on the indictment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no jury sworn: the "Where" gate fails (F46)
#ASSERT `s 317 the jury may give a general verdict of guilty or not guilty on the whole matter put in issue on the indictment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no such trial: the "Where" gate fails (F46)
#ASSERT `s 317 the jury shall not be required or directed by the judge to find the defendant guilty merely on proof of publication and of the sense ascribed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the bar applies inside the gate
#ASSERT `s 317 the jury shall not be required or directed by the judge to find the defendant guilty merely on proof of publication and of the sense ascribed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- outside the gate
#ASSERT `s 317 the judge may, in his discretion, give a direction or opinion to the jury on the matter in issue as in other criminal proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- inside the gate
#ASSERT `s 317 the judge may, in his discretion, give a direction or opinion to the jury on the matter in issue as in other criminal proceedings` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- outside the gate (F46)
#ASSERT `s 317 the jury may, on the issue, find a special verdict` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- inside the gate
#ASSERT `s 317 the jury may, on the issue, find a special verdict` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- outside the gate (F46)

-- #TRACE (read): the court directs the verdict at time 1 -> FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 316(2) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 316(2) direct a verdict of not guilty to be entered and discharge the accused` AT 1
